2026-09-27T10:19:17.3389305Z Update Note
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3389582Z ===========
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3389997Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3390404Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3390537Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3390834Z ================
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3391021Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3391251Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3391792Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3392125Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3392295Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3392692Z ====================================
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3392949Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3393144Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3393706Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3394203Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3395217Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3396124Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3396270Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3396946Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3398053Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3398531Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3399024Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3399695Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3399840Z Packages
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3400148Z ========
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3400318Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3402461Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3404782Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3405132Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3405911Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3407133Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3408307Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3492039Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3492911Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3493886Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3494059Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3494439Z ==========================
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3494663Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3496348Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3498294Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3499311Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3500597Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T10:19:17.3500904Z 
